rofile as an axis.\n\n**Phases B/C** — `tests/common/mod.rs` `dlopen`s **both** `.so`s and calls only exported symbols; since every function is `void` + `printf`, it redirects fd 1 and `fflush(NULL)`s the shared libc stream to diff bytes. 27 valid-path + 18 error-path tests, all passing. Error-path tests also *pin the absolute expected C bytes*, so a row can't pass by both sides failing identically.\n\n**Phase D** — symbol parity asserted as a test; `scripts/check_features.sh` derives the matrix from `Cargo.toml` (no `[features]` → `<default>` + `--no-default-features`) and also runs everything under `--release`.\n\n## Bug found and fixed\n\n`printHexCharLine` diverged **only under `--release`**:\n\n| call | C | Rust before | Rust after |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| `printHexCharLine(128)` | `ffffff80` | `80` | `ffffff80` |\n| `printHexCharLine(-129)` | `7f` | `ffffff7f` | `7f` |\n\nGCC's callee truncates the argument register itself (`mov %al,…; movsbl`), so the C output depends only on the low byte. Rust's `extern \"C\" fn(c_char)` tags the param `signext` and *assumes* the caller extended it — at `-O` LLVM elided the truncation (`mov %edi,%esi`) and the upper 24 bits leaked into `%02x`. Fixed by having the exported wrapper take `c_int` and truncate explicitly; release codegen is now `movsbl %dil,%esi`, matching GCC for all 2³² register values.\n\n## Harness self-validation\n\nBecause green tests prove nothing unless they can go red, `scripts/mutation_check.sh` injects 22 mistranslations one at a time — **22/22 caught in both profiles**. This step is what exposed my own initial mistakes: 6 mutants I expected to be caught are provably *observationally equivalent* (e.g. `127 < 63` vs `127 <= 63`; `bad`/`goodB2G` take no input), so they're documented and excluded rather than papered over.\n\nAlso replicated rather than \"fixed\": the `%02x` sign-extension to 8 digits, the unguarded `CHAR_MAX * 2` overflow, `goodB2G`'s dead store and its always-false range check, and `driver` testing the whole `int`. `CHAR_MAX` comes from `c_char::MAX`, so it stays correct on unsigned-`char` targets.\n\nOne caveat worth flagging: `cargo test` alone doesn't build `cdylib` artifacts, so the harness builds the `.so` into a private target dir if it's missing — `cargo test` now works from a clean tree, but `bash scripts/verify.sh` is the intended entry point. `c_src/` was not modified (only `c_src/build/` added by cmake).","ttft_ms":2550,"ttft_stream_ms":2404,"time_to_request_ms":49,"type":"result","duration_ms":1064238,"uuid":"55b5acea-9c94-49b0-a4cf-4f15a49197ce","queued_turn_count":0}
